  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 22 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Angiosarcomas are malignant, aggressive tumors that derive from the endothelium of blood vessels.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The condition is typically seen in elderly patients who present with regional pain and overlying skin changes.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with a biopsy showing malignant cells associated with vascular structures.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually wide surgical resection with radiation.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
